course: dictionary
lesson: 13615
title: Indeterminate: not clear or fixed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Indeterminate means not exactly known, fixed or clear. Its opposite is definite. Break the word into parts: in- means not, and determinate means fixed or certain, so indeterminate means not fixed or certain. «The old man had an indeterminate age, so I could not tell if he was forty or seventy.»
explain: Indeterminate often describes things you cannot pin down. «The colour of the sky at dusk was indeterminate, somewhere between grey and purple.» You can see it, but you cannot give it one clear name. Try swapping in vague: if the meaning still fits, you have found the right sense.
explain: In maths, an answer is indeterminate when the information is not enough to fix one value. «The equation x + y = 10 has an indeterminate answer, because x could be 3 and y 7, or x could be 5 and y 5.» Many answers are possible, so none of them is the single answer.
fact: Indeterminate means not exactly known, fixed or clear; vague.
fact: In- at the start of a word often means not, so indeterminate is the opposite of definite.
fact: «Indeterminate» can describe an age, a colour, a shape or a feeling that is hard to pin down.
fact: In maths, an answer is indeterminate when the information is not enough to give one single value.
fact: In law, an indeterminate sentence is a prison sentence with no fixed end date.
exercise: «The old man had an indeterminate age.» What does indeterminate mean here? | Written clearly on a sign | *Not clear, so you cannot tell his exact age | Very young | Very rich
exercise: In maths, «x + y = 10» has an indeterminate answer. Why? | There is no equals sign | The answer is exactly 10 | Only one answer is possible | *Many pairs of numbers could fit
exercise: What is a good synonym for indeterminate? | *vague | heavy | fast | bright
test: In law, what does an indeterminate sentence have? | *No fixed end date | A sentence written in pencil | A fixed end date of ten years | A fine only
test: «Her feelings were indeterminate; she could not say if she was happy or sad.» What does indeterminate mean? | Extremely happy | Very old | Very loud | *Not clear or fixed
exam: Which sentence uses indeterminate correctly? | The indeterminate boy ran faster than everyone and won the race | The answer was indeterminate because it was exactly 4 | *The colour of the sunset was indeterminate, somewhere between pink and orange | Indeterminate is a type of fruit
